														my 2 cp<br />
<br />
I think this guild has the potential to be great.  However, IMHO, it's up to the players just as much as the officers.<br />
<br />
From what I've seen and read here (keep in mind I've been off for a couple of months due to r/l stuff), the officers are definately doing their part.  If anyone has had a problem the officers, no matter who takes care of it, has done a bang-up job.<br />
<br />
Couple of comments about the last post that disturbed me:<br />
<br />
Web page - I was told that the web page was being worked on.  I offered my services to make a web page, and even offered to pay for the DNS name and host the web page on my own server.  Since the web page was already being worked on, I left it alone and never heard any news to the contrary that it wasn't.  That being said, I would be happy to help/work on and host a web page had I been asked.  Just because I'm not in EQ doesn't mean I can't touch my computer.<br />
<br />
Guild raids - The last raid we attempted was canceled due to lack of interest.  We had 4 people respond that they wanted to go, and that's not exactly enough to take out Unrest.  So we waited on ideas from other members, but nobody expressed any interest on these boards for something they would like to see raided.  If we are to put a raid up, we want it to be something that people want or need, not just any random zone because, as we've seen, people don't want to just gather to kill stuff anywhere.<br />
<br />
Invites - This is the one I can't figure out.  Are we just not grouping with quality people, or are they turning us down because we're not an &quot;uber&quot; guild?  If the latter, good.  We don't want to start off as an uber guild.  From my understanding, we want to be a mid-level guild where people can have fun before they hit their high lvls, and if they want to stick and grow with us that's great.  On another note, I do see people coming into this guild as others leave.  We may need to address the issue of how we treat each other in that case (again, I have not been on in a while so I haven't seen extensively how people are treated, but when I did log back on for a while people didn't seem to care or even say hi).						</td>
