														continued..... (ok, so it's a little more than 2cp)<br />
<br />
Officers leaving to do other things - I'm not exactly sure what you mean, but if it's in reference to taking R/L time off, that's just wrong to be mad about it.  I haven't seen in-game any officers leaving, but this may be exactly what Aam is speaking of.  Some officers may have just up and left without saying anything, I say good riddance if they are going to be that way, and they shouldn't have been made officers in the first place.  I understand that the guild was created with 10 people and needed more right away to stay afloat, but give officer status to those who have proven worthy time and time again.  I should hope that if I am found to not be living up to officer status that I will be asked to step down or be demoted.<br />
<br />
I still think this guild has potential.  The officers need to keep their part up, yes.  Other guilds that I've seen operate good are ones that TAKE INITIATIVE to GROUP WITH EACH OTHER.  This means running across the continent if necessary to group with that guy I haven't talked to much who's killing in Toxx Forest.  Easiest way to do this is put in /who all GUILD and see if there's anyone you don't know.  Then use /guild to say hi and see if they'd like a partner.  If they don't respond, keep trying.  If it seems they're ignoring you in /guild, shoot them a /tell, and if they answer that see why they're not listening to /guild.  That issue may have to go to an officer, because we don't want people ignoring /guild chat.  You can remain anonymous through emails, I know that all officers posted their email address.<br />
<br />
In summary, this guild still can be one of the greats.  I haven't seen how many we have lately, but we can fix that.  Just start inviting unguilded people in groups you may be in that are good people, and good at their class (when you're not able to find a guild group).  If you're not an officer, get one, and make it your personal duty to make them feel welcome enough to stay.  Remember that just because an officer may not be online, they still may be monitoring email and the message boards.  Put ideas out here on what you'd like to see.  After last time, at least for now, I for one am not going to just throw random raids out there that nobody's interested in, I want your ideas.  Web page is definately doable, just let me know, Aam.  I say we keep it alive, but it's up to all of you.						</td>
